# How every code point folds, in Unicode 17.0.0: the folded form texts are
# compared by ignoring case, and the next code point of the same letter.
# `casing.hero` reads them.
#
# Generated, never edited by hand: the Heroes program
# `generators/unicode_tables/` read the Unicode Character Database 17.0.0
# (https://www.unicode.org/Public/17.0.0/ucd/, fetched 2026-11-22), its
# files `CaseFolding.txt` and `UnicodeData.txt`, reduced them to ranges, held
# every lookup to the files' answer for each of the 1,114,112 code points, and
# wrote this module whole; its `check` command says whether this module is
# still what it writes.
#
# Each entry is one range, `first << 22 | last << 1 | step - 1`: the code
# points from `first` to `last`, every one where `step` is 1 and every second
# where it is 2, in ascending order.

# The ranges of code points whose folded form is one code point and not their
# lower case.
constant FOLD_RANGES: [i64]
    [
        759169386
        1606419198
        3510634122
        4034922372
        4093642656
        4097836962
        4114614186
